-- title:
--   Augmentation ideal spanned by g-1 over a generating set
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring and $G$ a group, and let $S \subseteq G$ be a subset whose generated subgroup $\mathrm{Subgroup.closure}\,S$ is all of $G$. Consider the group algebra $\mathcal{O}[G] =$ `MonoidAlgebra 𝒪 G` with its Mathlib bialgebra structure, whose counit algebra morphism `Bialgebra.counitAlgHom 𝒪 (MonoidAlgebra 𝒪 G)` is the augmentation $\mathcal{O}[G] \to \mathcal{O}$ sending a finitely supported function $x$ to the sum of its coefficients, equivalently $[g] \mapsto 1$ for $g \in G$. The assertion is an equality of ideals of $\mathcal{O}[G]$: the kernel of this augmentation equals `Ideal.span` of the image of $S$ under $g \mapsto [g] - 1$, where $[g]$ denotes `MonoidAlgebra.of 𝒪 G g`. Since $G$ is not assumed commutative, `Ideal` here is the left-module notion, so the span is the left ideal generated by the elements $[s] - 1$ with $s \in S$; the statement says that this left ideal is exactly the augmentation ideal.
--
--   This is the standard description of the augmentation ideal of a group ring as the ideal generated by $g - 1$ for $g$ running over any generating set of the group. It is used in the Taylor–Wiles patching apparatus, where it identifies the augmentation ideal of a diamond group ring $\mathcal{O}[\Delta_Q]$ with the ideal generated by $\delta_i - 1$ for chosen generators $\delta_i$; it is cited by [`Algebra.nonempty_patchingDatum_of_levelData`](thm.html#Algebra.nonempty_patchingDatum_of_levelData).
